"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkdocs_v_2=globalThis.webpackChunkdocs_v_2||[]).push([["6607"],{7735(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"v1.25.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/v1.25.0","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-13-v1.25.0.md","title":"ogen v1.25.0","description":"ogen v1.25.0 adds Swagger UI out of the box, works with Go 1.27.2, and fixes a dozen generator bugs.","date":"2026-11-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release"}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v1.25.0","title":"ogen v1.25.0","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false},"content":"ogen v1.25.0 adds Swagger UI out of the box, works with Go 1.27.2, and fixes a dozen generator bugs.\\nNine people made their first contribution to this release. Thank you!\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## Upgrade\\n\\n```console\\ngo get -tool github.com/ogen-go/ogen/cmd/ogen@v1.25.0\\ngo generate ./...\\n```\\n\\nBoth new features are opt-in. With the default config, the generated code changes only where the bug fixes below apply.\\n\\n## Swagger UI and the embedded spec\\n\\nTwo new features serve the OpenAPI document from the generated server ([#1775](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1775)):\\n\\n- `server/spec` embeds the document and generates `SpecJSON()`, `SpecYAML()`, `SpecHandler()` and the `WithDocs` server option.\\n- `server/swagger_ui` also serves Swagger UI. It implies `server/spec`.\\n\\n```yaml title=\\".ogen.yml\\"\\ngenerator:\\n  features:\\n    enable:\\n      - server/swagger_ui\\n```\\n\\n```go\\nsrv, err := api.NewServer(handler, api.WithDocs(\\"/docs\\"))\\n// http://localhost:8080/docs/             Swagger UI\\n// http://localhost:8080/docs/openapi.json the spec\\n```\\n\\nSwagger UI assets ship in the `swaggerui` package, which uses only the standard library.\\nTo load them from a CDN instead, use `WithDocsAssetsURL`.\\nThe `generator.spec_source` option (`auto`, `raw`, `expanded`) picks which document gets embedded:\\nthe original file, or a self-contained one with external `$ref`s resolved.\\n\\n## Struct aliases that keep methods\\n\\nWhen several content types or response codes share one schema, ogen generates a named type for each of them:\\n\\n```go\\ntype CreatePetOK Pet\\n```\\n\\nGo drops the methods of `Pet` from such a type.\\nThe new `schema/embed_struct_aliases` feature generates an embedding instead, so the methods carry over\\nand a single interface covers all the variants ([#1789](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1789)):\\n\\n```go\\ntype CreatePetOK struct {\\n\\tPet\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis changes the generated API (`CreatePetOK(pet)` becomes `CreatePetOK{pet}`), so the feature is off by default.\\n\\n## Go 1.27.2\\n\\nogen now builds and runs on Go 1.27.2 with JSON v2 enabled.\\n`GOEXPERIMENT=nojsonv2` is no longer needed ([#1774](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1774)).\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\nGenerated code that failed to compile:\\n\\n- Responses that share an inline header schema ([#1769](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1769)).\\n- Constant `uri` and other string formats ([#1752](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1752)).\\n- Object-level `x-ogen-validate` ([#1772](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1772)).\\n- `uniqueItems` arrays of MAC addresses ([#1788](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1788)).\\n- Webhooks with `security`. `NewWebhookServer` now takes a `SecurityHandler`, and `NewWebhookClient` takes a `SecuritySource`,\\n  but only when some webhook requires security ([#1771](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1771)).\\n- A security requirement that combines schemes with AND, one of them unsupported and listed in\\n  `ignore_not_implemented` ([#1760](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1760)).\\n\\nWrong behavior:\\n\\n- A `default` set next to a `$ref` applied to every use of that schema, not just that one ([#1758](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1758)).\\n- The client sent an empty value for unset optional parameters with structured content.\\n  Now it omits them ([#1741](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1741)).\\n- Decoding `null` into a nullable array kept the old value ([#1789](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1789)).\\n- `allOf` merging dropped `x-ogen-time-format` ([#1778](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1778)).\\n\\nSmaller fixes:\\n\\n- `min`/`max` conflict errors now name the real keywords, like `minLength` ([#1733](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1733)).\\n- A path like `/caf%e9/100%` crashed ogen with a panic. Now ogen reports an invalid escape ([#1732](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/pull/1732)).\\n\\nThe full list of changes is in the [release notes](https://github.com/ogen-go/ogen/releases/tag/v1.25.0)."}]}}')}}]);